# tune_v6 step A: the measurement fixes only, on top of tune_v5 (hover simulator, 2026-11-03,
# tools/sim/hover/RESULTS.md). Load together with the Pi change in companion/systemd/packet-cam.service
# (--imu-lag 0.053 --mount-fwd 0.127 --mount-down 0.101) and the new lua/hop_takeoff.lua.
# - INS_POS1/2: the IMUs are 5.8 cm above the CG (CAD; z also fitted from logs 35/43-45). With 0, a
#   rotation reads as a sideways acceleration (g - h w^2) x tilt: above 2.2 Hz it flips sign, and at
#   4.4 Hz the velocity D term saw ~3x the real motion = the growing 4.4 Hz ring of log 45.
# - PSC_NE_VEL_D 0: MUST go with INS_POS. With the true IMU position the D term sees the real
#   acceleration at 2-2.5 Hz, and VEL_D 1.0 there tipped the sim drone to 25 deg in 2 s (both seeds).
# - VISO_DELAY_MS 110: the camera fix is about 117 ms old when it reaches the FC (exposure -> t_cap
#   60 ms, fitted from the attitude-match error in logs 41-45; t_cap -> FC 57 ms). The FC dated it at
#   arrival - 71.5 ms; now arrival - 121.5 ms (the jitter correction takes 11.5 ms).
# - HTO_TRIM_P 0.85: hover trim for the takeoff script (logs 43/45 held +0.84..+0.87 deg). Without it
#   the drone lifts off into a 0.15 m/s^2 slide = the 2-3 cm hand-over offset. HTO_TRIM_* exist only
#   after the new hop_takeoff.lua has run once: load this file after that.
# Sim (11 plant/noise variants): stable in all (tune_v5 tipped over or diverged in 5 of 11); tilt
# wobble above 1 Hz 0.37-0.40 deg rms (tune_v5 0.62-0.69); hold 8-16 mm rms (tune_v5 10-12): the
# position hold is not better without the D term at these gains. tune_v6.parm is the full set.
# Before: INS_POS1/2_X/Y/Z 0, PSC_NE_VEL_D 1.0, VISO_DELAY_MS 60, HTO_TRIM_P/R (new, 0)
INS_POS1_X,-0.007
INS_POS1_Y,-0.001
INS_POS1_Z,-0.058
INS_POS2_X,-0.007
INS_POS2_Y,-0.001
INS_POS2_Z,-0.058
PSC_NE_VEL_D,0
VISO_DELAY_MS,110
HTO_TRIM_P,0.85
HTO_TRIM_R,0
